Ah, that was what you meant.

That was one of the big advantages of usenet in the early days. It was
the single place where public discussions happenend. But alas that has
obviously changed.

I don't think that it would work to unify discussion at one place,
though. We already have different roguelike forums (e.g. tome,
roguetemple, angband.oook.cz. NAO) and they don't show signs of
converging. not even the angband-related ones.


BTW, by technically superior I meant this:

A usenet reader is for newsgroups like a browser is for websites. One
program that interprets one standard and ideally that program fits
your needs best (with browsers it's not that ideally as there are
few different browsers in use, but with all the available extensions
browsers have gone a long way to be individually customized for each
user).

Unfortunately, there is no standard for forum postings that could work
similar like usenet does. Every forum software works differently, I
usually can't download the messages to read offline, some don't even
know threading or filtering, etc.

